From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] uxtheme: accept empty strings in SetWindowTheme

Purpose: let a window opt out of visual styles with SetWindowTheme(hwnd,
L"", L""), as documented. AddAtomW rejects an empty string, so Wine failed
the whole call with ERROR_INVALID_NAME and never sent WM_THEMECHANGED.
XP explorer turns theming off on the Start panel's log-off toolbar this way
and colours its labels through custom draw. Without the change the native
toolbar kept its Toolbar theme, ignored the custom colour and drew the
"log off" and "shut down" labels black instead of white.
Store a placeholder name that matches no theme class, so OpenThemeData
fails for that window and an empty sub-application name keeps the default
class. This changes Wine source only; no Microsoft binary is changed.
tests/window-theme-empty.c checks the HRESULT, WM_THEMECHANGED, the
OpenThemeData result and restoring the theme with NULL.
Reference: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/api/uxtheme/nf-uxtheme-setwindowtheme

diff --git a/dlls/uxtheme/system.c b/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
index 5da65ea..2f90dbb 100644
--- a/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
+++ b/dlls/uxtheme/system.c
@@ -592,7 +592,14 @@ static HRESULT UXTHEME_SetWindowProperty(HWND hwnd, ATOM aProp, LPCWSTR pszValue
     if(oldValue)
         DeleteAtom(oldValue);
     if(pszValue) {
-        ATOM atValue = AddAtomW(pszValue);
+        ATOM atValue;
+
+        /* AddAtomW rejects an empty string, but SetWindowTheme(hwnd, L"", L"")
+         * is the documented way to turn visual styles off for one window.
+         * Store a name that matches no theme class so OpenThemeData fails. */
+        if(!pszValue[0])
+            pszValue = L"0";
+        atValue = AddAtomW(pszValue);
         if(!atValue
            || !SetPropW(hwnd, (LPCWSTR)MAKEINTATOM(aProp), (LPWSTR)MAKEINTATOM(atValue))) {
             HRESULT hr = HRESULT_FROM_WIN32(GetLastError());
